  "handoffRules": [
    "Write learner-facing content in British English (en-GB), preserving exact API and database identifiers.",
    "Verify the programme, canonical module catalogue ID and week action before target-specific uploads or SQL.",
    "For several destination modules, create separate placement manifests with distinct week and component IDs.",
    "An actual module component must link to the selected module_catalogue_id and a week_id belonging to that same module.",
    "A new module requires a separately authorised learner assignment; programme and group labels alone do not assign it.",
    "Reusing a package must preserve its IDs and check ownership and checksums rather than overwrite a conflicting record.",
    "Every REPLACE value and example component ID must be reviewed before use.",
    "asset:// is a handoff reference only; replace it with a verified stable LMS URL before saving settings_json.",
    "fallbackAssetId, captionAssetId, quizRef and the outer envelope are proposed manifest fields, not existing backend fields.",
    "Do not mark the package ready while an asset, video integration or quiz database link is missing.",
    "Do not attach draft or incomplete content to a live learner module and assume Draft hides it.",
    "Quiz answer keys are authoring-only and must not be copied into learner-visible reading content.",
    "Keep settings_json.reflectionPrompt and components.Reflection_Question consistent for module components.",
    "No database write by the agent: produce exact SQL for the owner after files and IDs are verified.",
